{{- /* shakti is the Sunshine/Moonlight remote-desktop host (aditya is the
client side, moonlight-qt already installed there, no reason to also run
Sunshine on it). omarchy-install-service-sunshine would normally add this
line itself (enable_hyprland_autostart()), but its systemctl --user enable
--now sunshine call failed outright before reaching that point - the
actual unit shipped by the sunshine package is named
app-dev.lizardbyte.app.Sunshine.service, not "sunshine" (worth reporting
upstream - systemctl enable on that real name DOES register a "sunshine"
alias symlink via the unit's own [Install] Alias=, but only after the
first enable, so the script's assumption only works on a second run).
Added by hand on 2026-10-05 for that reason - not actually needed, since
systemd itself already relaunches the user service via
graphical-session.target.wants on every login, this is just for parity
with what the stock installer would have done. */}}
{{- if eq .chezmoi.hostname "shakti" }}
o.launch_on_start("sunshine")
{{- end }}
